  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the file set mapping the regression boundary:\n\n- **Babel side**: `plugin-proposal-decorators/src/index.ts` selects legacy vs stage-3 based on `version`/`legacy` option; `transformer-legacy.ts` implements the legacy visitor (which is what emits `Reflect.metadata`-compatible descriptor calls via `applyDecoratedDescriptor`); `plugin-transform-typescript/src/index.ts` and `preset-typescript/src/index.ts` establish plugin ordering (decorators plugin must run before/inherit from typescript's syntax plugin); `helper-create-class-features-plugin/src/decorators.ts` is the shared class-features engine both stage-3 and legacy paths funnel through; `plugin-syntax-decorators/src/index.ts` validates the `legacy` option.\n- **SWC side**: `crates/swc/src/config/mod.rs` is where `jsc.transform.legacyDecorator` and `decoratorMetadata` are read from `.swcrc`/config and wired into the pass pipeline \u2014 this is the customer-facing config surface that determines whether `Reflect.metadata` calls are emitted at all; `swc_ecma_transforms_typescript/{typescript.rs,config.rs}` show the TS strip pass itself does not carry decorator/metadata logic \u2014 that's gated separately by the `legacyDecorator`/`decoratorMetadata` flags in the top-level config, not implied by TS transform alone.\n\nThe divergence: Babel's `legacy: true` on `plugin-proposal-decorators` implicitly emits Reflect-metadata-compatible descriptors as part of the legacy visitor: it's inseparable from turning legacy mode on. SWC treats `legacyDecorator` and `decoratorMetadata` as two independent boolean flags in `jsc.transform`; setting only `legacyDecorator: true` (matching Babel's `legacy: true` semantics) does **not** imply metadata emission \u2014 `decoratorMetadata` must be explicitly set `true` as well, and it requires `experimentalDecorators`-equivalent config plus `emitDecoratorMetadata` in tsconfig to be honored. A swc config migrated from a Babel `legacy: true` setup that only sets `legacyDecorator: true` silently drops all `design:type`/`design:paramtypes`/`design:returntype` metadata, which is exactly the customer's failure: decorators still execute (class construction unaffected) but Nest's `Reflect.getMetadata` calls return `undefined` because no metadata was ever emitted.",
